u]-H[X'\mid Z';
u]$ and $H[Y';
u]-H[Y'\mid W';
u]$. The goal is now an inequality between the displayed entropy expressions.

Apply `condEntropy_le_entropy` to $X'-Y'$ conditioned on $\langle Z',W'angle$ under $
u$, giving $H[X'-Y'\mid \langle Z',W'angle;
u]\le H[X'-Y';
u]$; the required measurability and finite-range hypotheses are supplied by the construction. The remaining inequality is linear after the $H[X']$ and $H[Y']$ terms cancel, and `linarith` closes it from this bound, with the nonnegativity facts for $H[Z';
